From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 05:06:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PC5: frame generation in RADV's libvulkan.prx, 30 fps shown
 at 60

With a ps5-framegen checkout (--framegen), libvulkan.prx links its
interpolator (FSR3's optical flow and frame interpolation) and wraps the
device, queues, swapchains and presents when PW_PC5_FRAMEGEN=1: the game is
held at half the display's rate and a frame made between each two of its
frames is presented before each one. It engages after 8 frames on time and
shows the game's frames as they come when it falls behind.

Without a checkout every entry point passes through, as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W9bbTPMqftZ2Yv6sJzUsWv
